==============================================================================
PART 3: Canonical centering tau=(2j+1)/(2w) -- is it FORCED into G_C?
==============================================================================
Perfect middle of w-band: tau=(2j+1)/(2w) gives ||w tau||=1/2 (max possible).
Question: does the easy core's structure FORCE some such center into G_C?
Also relate to dihedral clock events (14k +/- 1)/(14 v).

--- core {1..11,13} ---
  core1..11,13 + w=84            w=  84: #band-centers in (0,1)=84, #inside G_C=0
      NO band-center of w lies in G_C (centering tau not core-forced).
  core1..11,13 + w=168           w= 168: #band-centers in (0,1)=168, #inside G_C=0
      NO band-center of w lies in G_C (centering tau not core-forced).
  core1..11,13 + w=14            w=  14: #band-centers in (0,1)=14, #inside G_C=0
      NO band-center of w lies in G_C (centering tau not core-forced).
  core1..11,13 + w=28            w=  28: #band-centers in (0,1)=28, #inside G_C=0
      NO band-center of w lies in G_C (centering tau not core-forced).
  core1..11,13 + w=42            w=  42: #band-centers in (0,1)=42, #inside G_C=4
      best center tau=1/12       ~0.083333  core-gap=1/12     ~0.08333  full-gap(min over S)=1/12     ~0.08333
      dihedral-clock forms (14k+/-1)/(14 v): none small

